\section{Physical Inductive Biases Fail}
\label{sec:fails}

We inject physical structure into the shared $192$-dimensional latent through five mechanisms spanning the design space---from pinning \emph{what the state is} to constraining \emph{how it evolves}, with and without labels (Table~\ref{tab:mechanisms}). All variants run on top of free rollout, i.e., they must beat an already strong training protocol, which is the deployment-relevant question.

\begin{table}[t]
\centering
\small
\begin{tabular}{@{}p{2.1cm}p{2.5cm}cc@{}}
\toprule
Mechanism & Constrains & Labels & Form \\
\midrule
Fixed slot & state value ($\latp{=}$pos.) & yes & --- \\
Probe & state readout & yes & --- \\
Kinematic head & evolution & yes & fixed/MLP \\
Consistency & evolution (velocity) & yes & form-free \\
Label-free prior & evolution & \textbf{no} & 2nd-order \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\caption{Five physical-structure injection mechanisms. ``Fixed/MLP'' includes the exact gravitational form $a{=}g$ with a single learnable parameter. The label-free prior requires the slot to evolve under smooth second-order dynamics without ground-truth grounding.}
\label{tab:mechanisms}
\end{table}

\subsection{Post-hoc Injection: Every Mechanism Hurts}
\label{sec:posthoc}

Table~\ref{tab:injection} reports the hardest clean-split latent nMSE for each mechanism against the pure free-rollout baseline. Three observations stand out. First, \emph{correct physics does not help}: on parabola, the strict gravitational head---the ground-truth functional form, with only the gravity constant learned---degrades error from $0.127$ to $0.173$, no better than an unconstrained MLP head ($0.178$). Second, \emph{labels do not help}: the label-free prior degrades all three domains (collision most, $0.393\!\to\!0.653$), but so does its fully grounded counterpart with perfect position labels ($0.131\!\to\!0.166$ on uniform). Third, \emph{combinations do not rescue}: probe supervision alone is harmful ($0.131\!\to\!0.167$; confirmed in pixel space, $20.41\!\to\!19.83$\,dB on both-OOD), adding it to the reweighted slot yields nothing beyond seed noise in latent space ($0.125$ vs.\ $0.132\pm0.014$) while its pixel rollout falls below even the baseline ($20.02$ vs.\ $20.41$\,dB), and extending the slot to also carry velocity is the worst uniform variant of all ($0.114\!\to\!0.207$). The form-free consistency loss, designed specifically for collision impulses, fails worst exactly there ($0.57$--$0.64$ vs.\ $0.393$), and fails on the smooth domains too ($0.151$ vs.\ $0.131$; $0.147$ vs.\ $0.127$).

