\subsection{Post-hoc Injection: Every Mechanism Hurts}
\label{sec:posthoc}

Table~\ref{tab:injection} reports the hardest clean-split latent nMSE for each mechanism against the pure free-rollout baseline---$30$ mechanism--domain cells in total. Three observations stand out. First, \emph{correct physics does not help}: on parabola, the strict gravitational head---the ground-truth functional form, with only the gravity constant learned---degrades error from $0.127$ to $0.173$, no better than an unconstrained MLP head ($0.178$). Second, \emph{labels do not help}: the label-free prior degrades all three domains (collision most, $0.393\!\to\!0.653$), and so does its fully grounded counterpart with perfect position labels ($0.131\!\to\!0.166$ on uniform; $0.393\!\to\!0.525$ on collision). Third, \emph{combinations do not rescue}: probe supervision alone is harmful ($0.131\!\to\!0.167$ on uniform, confirmed in pixel space, $20.41\!\to\!19.83$\,dB; $0.393\!\to\!0.647$ on collision), and adding it to the reweighted slot yields parity at best ($0.125$ vs.\ $0.132\pm0.014$ on uniform; $0.127$ on parabola) or clear damage ($0.607$ on collision), while its pixel rollout falls below even the baseline ($20.02$ vs.\ $20.41$\,dB). The form-free consistency loss, designed specifically for collision impulses, fails worst exactly there ($0.57$--$0.64$ vs.\ $0.393$), and fails on the smooth domains too ($0.151$ vs.\ $0.131$; $0.147$ vs.\ $0.127$).

Across the grid, $28$ of $30$ cells fail to improve on the baseline, and the two apparent exceptions---both single-seed, both on parabola's \rmood{} split---do not survive scrutiny. Probe-only parabola reads $0.115$, exactly the bottom of the baseline's own seed range ($0.115$--$0.127$): seed noise. The slot carrying position$+$velocity reads $0.093$ on parabola while being the \emph{worst} uniform variant ($0.114\!\to\!0.207$) and clearly harmful on collision ($0.621$); we replicate this single cell across seeds before reading anything into it, and note that a mechanism whose sign flips across the two smooth domains cannot support a robustness claim in any case.

